// Negative fixture (guard reject): a fact proven non-null on only ONE
// branch of an if does not survive the join — reading the nullable after
// the if must be rejected before the program runs (meet-at-join
// flow concept: maybe-null wins unless proven on every
// completing path).
// Expected pre-run diagnostic:
//   GuardError: NullValueException ...: y: nullable value x used without a
//   null check (use ??)

int? src() << null;

void main() {
    int? x = src();
    if (src() != null) {
        x = 1;
    }
    int y = x;
    printline(y);
}
